    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_done": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I know when the salmon is done?",
            "text": "<p>Small pieces cook quickly. Erica roasts them for 15&ndash;20 minutes at 400&deg;F, until done to her liking: check at 12. The FDA conservatively suggests cooking seafood to an internal temperature of 145&nbsp;&deg;F.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_thaw": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I thaw the salmon?",
            "text": "<p>In the refrigerator, in its sealed pack, overnight. Never on the counter or in warm water. Pat it dry before you cut and season it, so the honey coats it evenly.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_squash": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need to peel the delicata?",
            "text": "<p>No. Delicata skin is thin and softens in the oven. Halve it lengthwise, scoop out the seeds, and cut it into thin half-moons.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_ahead": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I make it ahead?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Cook the quinoa and lentils, roast the squash and whisk the tahini ahead, and keep them in the fridge separately. The tahini thickens as it sits: loosen it with a splash of water. Roast the salmon fresh, or reheat it gently.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_gf": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it gluten- and dairy-free?",
            "text": "<p>As written, yes. Check the labels on your tahini, spices and cashews if you are cooking for an allergy, and swap the cashews for pumpkin seeds if you need it nut-free.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_more": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I make it for four?",
            "text": "<p>Use a 4-Pack of Atlantic Salmon and double everything else. Use two baking sheets so the squash and salmon roast instead of steaming.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q_done",
        "q_thaw",
        "q_squash",
        "q_ahead",
